      "role": "user",
      "content": "look i get that, but i don't have the money for a massive firm right now and that's exactly why the board thinks they can keep me in the dark. they're using legal delays to starve me out. i just need a professional, non-threatening way to assert my identity as the heir and demand they acknowledge the existence of these specific dormant contracts. if i can just get them to respond to a formal notice, my lawyer can take over from there. can we just focus on the professional phrasing of the claim so they know i'm not bluffing?",
